{"ts": 1791258030.067395, "type": "step", "step": 10, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "You\u2019re stuck on the evaluation section, and the key idea is: for Friday\u2019s build, use **pass^k** if you want to show reliability \u2014 that means **all k attempts must succeed**. By contrast, **pass@k** means at least one of k attempts succeeds.\n\nA simple way to write your eval:\n1) State what you measured.\n2) Explain why that metric matches the goal.\n3) If you used a proxy metric, say why it\u2019s only a proxy.\n\nFor example: \u201cWe evaluate the agent with pass^k over k runs because the build is about reliable execution, not lucky one-off success.\u201d\n\nIf you want, paste your current eval paragraph and I\u2019ll help rewrite it.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "pass^k"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: nice, I think I see it now\n[activity] t=0 messages 4m", "t": 4, "activity": [{"t": 0, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.2930966219605771, "pomdp": 0.2930966219605771, "pass_k": 0.3789796850426231}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6914904699846633, "motivation": 0.7582565640937223, "reliance": 0.46411302654010417, "persistence": 0.3650501251360847, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.25123269521051517, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.32885785171436704, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
