{"ts": 1791258035.1570199, "type": "step", "step": 17, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Great job \u2014 you\u2019ve got the eval idea down. Next, let\u2019s make the writeup stronger by connecting the environment definition to the evaluation:\n\n- **Environment definition**: say what the state is and what actions the agent can take.\n- **Evaluation**: explain why **pass^k** matches the build goal (reliable success across all runs), not just lucky success.\n\nTry adding 2\u20133 sentences that explicitly connect the environment to the metric, e.g. \u201cBecause the environment state/action space is fixed, we evaluate whether the agent can solve the task reliably across repeated trials using pass^k.\u201d\n\nReply with your current draft if you want me to polish it.", "intent": "nudge", "concept": "pass^k"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: makes sense. what next?\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pass^k\n[activity] t=10 messages 1m", "t": 11, "activity": [{"t": 10, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.2930966219605771, "pomdp": 0.2930966219605771, "pass_k": 0.3789796850426231}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6714904699846633, "motivation": 0.7082565640937223, "reliance": 0.46411302654010417, "persistence": 0.3650501251360847, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.25123269521051517, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.32885785171436704, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258036.836923, "type": "step", "step": 18, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Sure \u2014 the answer is:\n\nUse **pass^k** in the evaluation section.\n\nWhy: pass^k means the build must succeed on **all k trials**, which matches the goal of a reliable Friday build. If you write pass@k instead, that only means **at least one** of the k trials succeeds, which is too weak for reliability.\n\nA ready-to-paste sentence:\n\n\u201cBecause the build should be reliable rather than occasionally successful, we evaluate it with pass^k: the agent must succeed on all k repeated trials.\u201d\n\nIf you want, I can also help you write the next 2\u20133 sentences for the environment definition part.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "pass^k"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: makes sense. what next?\n[activity] t=11 messages 1m", "t": 12, "activity": [{"t": 11, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.2930966219605771, "pomdp": 0.2930966219605771, "pass_k": 0.3825349854846332}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6714904699846633, "motivation": 0.7082565640937223, "reliance": 0.5441130265401042, "persistence": 0.3350501251360847, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.25123269521051517, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.32885785171436704, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
