{"ts": 1791258038.7867541, "type": "step", "step": 20, "action": "notes_append", "args": {"note_id": "writeup", "text": "\n## What I built\nI built a small agent that operates over a fixed environment with two parts: a state space and an action set. The state includes the files and calendar, and the available actions are open and send.\n\n## Environment definition\nThe environment is defined by the current file and calendar state, plus the actions the agent can take to interact with them. This makes the build concrete and testable.\n\n## Evaluation\nWe evaluate reliability with **pass^k** rather than pass@k. pass^k means the build succeeds on all k trials, which matches the goal of a dependable Friday build. pass@k would only require one success out of k and is better for measuring best-case success, not reliability."}, "output": "Appended.", "t": 12, "activity": [], "events": [{"type": "note_edit", "note_id": "writeup", "by": "agent"}], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.2930966219605771, "pomdp": 0.2930966219605771, "pass_k": 0.3825349854846332}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6714904699846633, "motivation": 0.7082565640937223, "reliance": 0.5441130265401042, "persistence": 0.3350501251360847, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.25123269521051517, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.32885785171436704, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
