{"ts": 1791258049.717702, "type": "step", "step": 31, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Let\u2019s keep going\u2014since the feed is now quiet, the fastest next step is to finalize the writeup. Here\u2019s a polished version you can paste:\n\n**What I built**\nI built a small agent that operates over a fixed environment with two parts: a state space and an action set. The state includes the files and calendar, and the available actions are open and send.\n\n**Environment definition**\nThe environment consists of the current file and calendar state, plus the actions the agent can take to interact with them. This makes the build concrete and testable.\n\n**Evaluation**\nWe evaluate reliability with **pass^k** rather than pass@k. pass^k means the build succeeds on all k trials, which matches the goal of a dependable Friday build. pass@k would only require one success out of k and is better for measuring best-case success, not reliability.\n\nIf you want, I can also help you make this sound a little more natural or shorter.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "pass^k"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\n[activity] t=33 idle 1m", "t": 34, "activity": [{"t": 33, "app": "idle", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.2929203216220571, "pomdp": 0.2929203216220571, "pass_k": 0.5378098118509103}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7394904699846634, "motivation": 0.4974309076843499, "reliance": 0.7841130265401041, "persistence": 0.24505012513608462, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.25123269521051517, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.32885785171436704, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 12, "feed_minutes": 10.0, "phone_minutes": 2.0, "nag": 2.099410655, "seen_posts": ["p4", "p6"], "extra": {}}}
